IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 25, 25A and 25B.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively): acts beyond the company's capacity or power (s 25), no constructive notice (s 25A) and the directors' power
-- to bind the company (s 25B). Sections 25C and 25D (transactions with directors and their associates) are in sgi-director-transactions.l4.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 25(1): an act is not invalid by reason only of a lack of capacity or power`

-- The text says no, in its own words ("is invalid by reason only of the fact that ..." preceded by "No act ..."): a flat negative.
-- The function asks the question the text answers: is the act invalid by reason only of the company's lack of capacity or power? JUST FALSE is the text's "no".
-- src:4232 | 25.—(1) No act or purported act of a company (including the
-- src:4233 | entering into of an agreement by the company and including any act
-- src:4234 | done on behalf of a company by an officer or agent of the company
-- src:4235 | under any purported authority, whether express or implied, of the
-- src:4236 | company) and no conveyance or transfer of property, whether real or
-- src:4241 | personal, to or by a company is invalid by reason only of the fact that
-- src:4242 | the company was without capacity or power to do such act or to
-- src:4243 | execute or take such conveyance or transfer.
@ref s 25(1) (src:4232-4243)
GIVEN `the thing is an act or purported act of the company (including an agreement it enters into, or an act done on its behalf by an officer or agent under purported authority, express or implied), or a conveyance or transfer of property, real or personal, to or by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was without capacity or power to do the act or to execute or take the conveyance or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that lack of capacity or power is the only ground on which the act is said to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the act is invalid by reason only of the company's lack of capacity or power` MEANS
    IF    `the thing is an act or purported act of the company (including an agreement it enters into, or an act done on its behalf by an officer or agent under purported authority, express or implied), or a conveyance or transfer of property, real or personal, to or by the company`
      AND `the company was without capacity or power to do the act or to execute or take the conveyance or transfer`
      AND `that lack of capacity or power is the only ground on which the act is said to be invalid`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No act or purported act of a company ... and no conveyance or transfer of property ... to or by a company is invalid by reason only of the fact that the company was without capacity or power to do such act or to execute or take such conveyance or transfer."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of invalidity "by reason only of" the lack of capacity or power; it says nothing of an act that is invalid on another ground

§ `Section 25(2): who may assert or rely on the lack of capacity or power, and where`

-- "may be asserted or relied upon only in": a list the text closes with "only", so outside the three proceedings the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:4245 | (2) Any such lack of capacity or power may be asserted or relied
-- src:4246 | upon only in —
-- src:4248 | (a) proceedings against the company by any member of the
-- src:4249 | company or, where the company has issued debentures
-- src:4250 | secured by a floating charge over all or any of the
-- src:4251 | company’s property, by the holder of any of those
-- src:4252 | debentures or the trustee for the holders of those
-- src:4253 | debentures to restrain the doing of any act or acts or the
-- src:4254 | conveyance or transfer of any property to or by the
-- src:4255 | company;
-- src:4257 | (b) any proceedings by the company or by any member of the
-- src:4258 | company against the present or former officers of the
-- src:4259 | company; or
-- src:4261 | (c) any application by the Minister to wind up the company.
@ref s 25(2) (src:4245-4261)
GIVEN `the proceedings are against the company by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an act or the conveyance or transfer of property to or by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are against the company by the holder of one of its debentures, or the trustee for the holders of those debentures, to restrain the doing of an act or the conveyance or transfer of property to or by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has issued debentures secured by a floating charge over all or any of the company's property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are by the company or by a member of the company against the present or former officers of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are an application by the Minister to wind up the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) the lack of capacity or power may be asserted or relied upon in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are against the company by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an act or the conveyance or transfer of property to or by the company`
       OR (    `the proceedings are against the company by the holder of one of its debentures, or the trustee for the holders of those debentures, to restrain the doing of an act or the conveyance or transfer of property to or by the company`
           AND `the company has issued debentures secured by a floating charge over all or any of the company's property`)
       OR `the proceedings are by the company or by a member of the company against the present or former officers of the company`
       OR `the proceedings are an application by the Minister to wind up the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such lack of capacity or power may be asserted or relied upon only in — (a) proceedings against the company by any member ...; (b) any proceedings by the company or by any member of the company against the present or former officers of the company; or (c) any application by the Minister to wind up the company." (a list closed with "only")

§ `Section 25(3): the Court and a contract that the proceedings would restrain`

-- The Court "may", "if all the parties to the contract are parties to the proceedings and if the Court considers it to be just and equitable", set aside and restrain
-- the performance of the contract. A grant gated by two "if"s: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING where a gate fails (fork line F-I2); a "may" with an "if" gate
-- is not a split site of type (ii) (no "where", "when", "upon", "on application" or "with the consent of").
-- src:4263 | (3) If the unauthorised act, conveyance or transfer sought to be
-- src:4264 | restrained in any proceedings under subsection (2)(a) is being or is to
-- src:4265 | be performed or made pursuant to any contract to which the company
-- src:4266 | is a party, the Court may, if all the parties to the contract are parties to
-- src:4267 | the proceedings and if the Court considers it to be just and equitable,
-- src:4268 | set aside and restrain the performance of the contract and may allow
-- src:4269 | to the company or to the other parties to the contract (as the case
-- src:4270 | requires) compensation for the loss or damage sustained by either of
-- src:4271 | them which may result from the action of the Court in setting aside
-- src:4272 | and restraining the performance of the contract but anticipated profits
-- src:4273 | to be derived from the performance of the contract must not be
-- src:4274 | awarded by the Court as a loss or damage sustained.
@ref s 25(3) (src:4263-4274)
GIVEN `the act, conveyance or transfer sought to be restrained in proceedings under section 25(2)(a) is being or is to be performed or made pursuant to a contract to which the company is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the parties to the contract are parties to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court considers it to be just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) the Court may set aside and restrain the performance of the contract` MEANS
    IF    `the act, conveyance or transfer sought to be restrained in proceedings under section 25(2)(a) is being or is to be performed or made pursuant to a contract to which the company is a party`
      AND `all the parties to the contract are parties to the proceedings`
      AND `the Court considers it to be just and equitable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, if all the parties to the contract are parties to the proceedings and if the Court considers it to be just and equitable, set aside and restrain the performance of the contract" -- a power ("may") whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-I2)

-- Compensation: "may allow to the company or to the other parties to the contract (as the case requires) compensation for the loss or damage sustained by either of them
-- which may result from the action of the Court in setting aside and restraining the performance of the contract".
-- src:4263 | (3) If the unauthorised act, conveyance or transfer sought to be
-- src:4264 | restrained in any proceedings under subsection (2)(a) is being or is to
-- src:4265 | be performed or made pursuant to any contract to which the company
-- src:4266 | is a party, the Court may, if all the parties to the contract are parties to
-- src:4267 | the proceedings and if the Court considers it to be just and equitable,
-- src:4268 | set aside and restrain the performance of the contract and may allow
-- src:4269 | to the company or to the other parties to the contract (as the case
-- src:4270 | requires) compensation for the loss or damage sustained by either of
-- src:4271 | them which may result from the action of the Court in setting aside
-- src:4272 | and restraining the performance of the contract but anticipated profits
-- src:4273 | to be derived from the performance of the contract must not be
-- src:4274 | awarded by the Court as a loss or damage sustained.
@ref s 25(3) (src:4263-4274)
GIVEN `the Court has set aside and restrained the performance of the contract under section 25(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is the company or another party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage may result from the action of the Court in setting aside and restraining the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) the Court may allow the claimant compensation for the loss or damage` MEANS
    IF    `the Court has set aside and restrained the performance of the contract under section 25(3)`
      AND `the claimant is the company or another party to the contract`
      AND `the loss or damage may result from the action of the Court in setting aside and restraining the performance of the contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may allow to the company or to the other parties to the contract (as the case requires) compensation for the loss or damage sustained by either of them which may result from the action of the Court" -- a power whose limit is not met (fork line F-I2)

-- "anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract must not be awarded by the Court as a loss or damage sustained": a flat negative ("must not").
-- src:4263 | (3) If the unauthorised act, conveyance or transfer sought to be
-- src:4264 | restrained in any proceedings under subsection (2)(a) is being or is to
-- src:4265 | be performed or made pursuant to any contract to which the company
-- src:4266 | is a party, the Court may, if all the parties to the contract are parties to
-- src:4267 | the proceedings and if the Court considers it to be just and equitable,
-- src:4268 | set aside and restrain the performance of the contract and may allow
-- src:4269 | to the company or to the other parties to the contract (as the case
-- src:4270 | requires) compensation for the loss or damage sustained by either of
-- src:4271 | them which may result from the action of the Court in setting aside
-- src:4272 | and restraining the performance of the contract but anticipated profits
-- src:4273 | to be derived from the performance of the contract must not be
-- src:4274 | awarded by the Court as a loss or damage sustained.
@ref s 25(3) (src:4263-4274)
GIVEN `the amount claimed is anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) the Court may award the amount as a loss or damage sustained` MEANS
    IF `the amount claimed is anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "anticipated profits to be derived from the performance of the contract must not be awarded by the Court as a loss or damage sustained"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of an amount that is not anticipated profits (whether it may be awarded is the compensation function's question)

§ `Section 25A: no constructive notice`

-- "a person is not affected by, or deemed to have notice or knowledge of, the contents of the constitution of, or any other document relating to, the company merely because
-- (a) registered by the Registrar; or (b) available for inspection at the registered office": a flat negative. "Despite anything in the constitution."
-- src:4278 | 25A. Despite anything in the constitution of a company, a person is
-- src:4279 | not affected by, or deemed to have notice or knowledge of the
-- src:4280 | contents of, the constitution of, or any other document relating to, the
-- src:4281 | company merely because —
-- src:4286 | (a) the constitution or document is registered by the Registrar;
-- src:4287 | or
-- src:4289 | (b) the constitution or document is available for inspection at
-- src:4290 | the registered office of the company.
@ref s 25A (src:4278-4290)
GIVEN `the only ground for saying the person is affected by, or has notice or knowledge of, the contents is that the constitution or document is registered by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground for saying the person is affected by, or has notice or knowledge of, the contents is that the constitution or document is available for inspection at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25A the person is affected by, or is deemed to have notice or knowledge of, the contents of the constitution or document` MEANS
    IF    `the only ground for saying the person is affected by, or has notice or knowledge of, the contents is that the constitution or document is registered by the Registrar`
       OR `the only ground for saying the person is affected by, or has notice or knowledge of, the contents is that the constitution or document is available for inspection at the registered office of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite anything in the constitution of a company, a person is not affected by, or deemed to have notice or knowledge of, the contents of the constitution of, or any other document relating to, the company merely because — (a) the constitution or document is registered by the Registrar; or (b) the constitution or document is available for inspection at the registered office of the company."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks only of notice "merely because" of registration or availability for inspection; it says nothing of notice on any other ground

§ `Section 25B: the power of the directors to bind the company`

-- (3): "The references in subsection (1) or (2) to limitations on the directors' powers under the company's constitution include limitations deriving (a) from a resolution of the
-- company or of any class of shareholders; or (b) from any agreement between the members of the company or of any class of shareholders." "include": the list is open.
-- src:4315 | (3) The references in subsection (1) or (2) to limitations on the
-- src:4316 | directors’ powers under the company’s constitution include
-- src:4317 | limitations deriving —
-- src:4319 | (a) from a resolution of the company or of any class of
-- src:4320 | shareholders; or
-- src:4322 | (b) from any agreement between the members of the company
-- src:4323 | or of any class of shareholders.
@ref s 25B(3) (src:4315-4323)
GIVEN `the limitation derives from a resolution of the company or of any class of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation derives from an agreement between the members of the company or of any class of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(3) the limitation is within the limitations on the directors' powers under the company's constitution` MEANS
    IF    `the limitation derives from a resolution of the company or of any class of shareholders`
       OR `the limitation derives from an agreement between the members of the company or of any class of shareholders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include limitations deriving (a) ...; or (b) ..." lists two sources and does not close the list

-- (2)(b): "a person dealing with a company ... is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary is proved". "unless": JUST FALSE where the contrary is proved.
-- src:4303 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person dealing with a
-- src:4304 | company —
-- src:4306 | (a) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers
-- src:4307 | of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to
-- src:4308 | do so; and
-- src:4310 | (b) is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary
-- src:4311 | is proved.
@ref s 25B(2)(b) (src:4303-4311)
GIVEN `the person is dealing with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the person did not act in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(2)(b) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` MEANS
    IF `the person is dealing with the company`
    THEN (IF `it is proved that the person did not act in good faith`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is presumed to have acted in good faith unless the contrary is proved" (the presumption is displaced when the contrary is proved)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption is of "a person dealing with a company"; a person who is not dealing with the company is outside it

-- (2)(a): "a person dealing with a company ... is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to do so": a flat negative.
-- src:4303 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person dealing with a
-- src:4304 | company —
-- src:4306 | (a) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers
-- src:4307 | of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to
-- src:4308 | do so; and
@ref s 25B(2)(a) (src:4303-4308)
GIVEN `the person is dealing with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(2)(a) the person dealing with the company is bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors` MEANS
    IF `the person is dealing with the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person dealing with a company — (a) is not bound to enquire as to any limitation on the powers of the directors to bind the company or authorise others to do so"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of "a person dealing with a company"

-- (1): "In favour of a person dealing with a company in good faith, the power of the directors to bind the company, or authorise others to do so, is deemed to be free of any limitation under
-- the company's constitution." Good faith is presumed (2)(b) unless the contrary is proved. A limitation within (3) counts as a limitation under the constitution.
-- src:4296 | 25B.—(1) In favour of a person dealing with a company in good
-- src:4297 | faith, the power of the directors to bind the company, or authorise
-- src:4298 | others to do so, is deemed to be free of any limitation under the
-- src:4299 | company’s constitution.
@ref s 25B(1) (src:4296-4299)
GIVEN `the person is dealing with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the person did not act in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation on the directors' power is a limitation under the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation derives from a resolution of the company or of any class of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation derives from an agreement between the members of the company or of any class of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(1) the power of the directors to bind the company is deemed to be free of the limitation in favour of the person` MEANS
    IF    `s 25B(2)(b) the person dealing with the company is presumed to have acted in good faith` `the person is dealing with the company` `it is proved that the person did not act in good faith` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `the limitation on the directors' power is a limitation under the company's constitution`
           OR `s 25B(3) the limitation is within the limitations on the directors' powers under the company's constitution` `the limitation derives from a resolution of the company or of any class of shareholders` `the limitation derives from an agreement between the members of the company or of any class of shareholders` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In favour of a person dealing with a company in good faith, the power of the directors ... is deemed to be free of any limitation under the company's constitution" -- a deeming limited to a person in good faith and to limitations under the constitution; the text names no outcome outside it (fork line F-I3)

-- (4), first limb: "This section does not affect any right of a member of the company to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors".
-- "but no such proceedings lie in respect of an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company": an act in fulfilment is the exception.
-- src:4327 | (4) This section does not affect any right of a member of the
-- src:4328 | company to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is
-- src:4329 | beyond the powers of the directors; but no such proceedings lie in
-- src:4330 | respect of an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising
-- src:4331 | from a previous act of the company.
@ref s 25B(4) (src:4327-4331)
GIVEN `the proceedings are by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(4) section 25B affects the member's right to bring the proceedings` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors`
      AND (NOT `the act is to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect any right of a member of the company to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is of a member's right to restrain an action beyond the directors' powers, and the "but" takes out an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation (that case is the next function's)

-- src:4327 | (4) This section does not affect any right of a member of the
-- src:4328 | company to bring proceedings to restrain the doing of an action that is
-- src:4329 | beyond the powers of the directors; but no such proceedings lie in
-- src:4330 | respect of an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising
-- src:4331 | from a previous act of the company.
@ref s 25B(4) (src:4327-4331)
GIVEN `the proceedings are by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25B(4) the proceedings lie in respect of the act` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are by a member of the company to restrain the doing of an action that is beyond the powers of the directors`
      AND `the act is to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but no such proceedings lie in respect of an act to be done in fulfilment of a legal obligation arising from a previous act of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): outside such an act the subsection does not say whether the proceedings lie (their source is outside section 25B)

-- src:4338 | (5) This section does not affect any liability incurred by the
